    \n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────                                                           \n> what is this setting? \"usage = { color_attachment = true },\" isn't that the default?                                 \n                                                                                                                       \n● Explored 1 file (gfx.odin) (ctrl+o to expand)                                                                        \n                                                                                                                       \n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────                                                           \n> what is this setting? \"usage = { color_attachment = true },\" isn't that the default?                                 \n                                                                                                                       \n● Explored 1 file (gfx.odin) (ctrl+o to expand)                                                                        \n                                                                                                                       \n  No. The default image usage in sokol-gfx is .immutable = true (gfx.odin:4252).                                       \n                                                                                                                       \n  An immutable image is a static read-only texture uploaded from the CPU (like a loaded PNG or sprite sheet) and       \n  requires initial data:                                                                                               \n                                                                                                                       \n    // Default image: read-only static texture                                                                         \n    usage = { immutable = true }                      