ldn't it be in range 0 -> 4?                         \n▸ Thought for 7s, 636 tokens                                                                                           \n  Initial hypothesis: The UV mapping likely extends beyond the 0-1 range to accommodate the position coordinates' w... \n  The screen span is 2 units wide: from -1.0 to +1.0.                                                                  \n                                                                                                                       \n  To map the screen [-1.0, 1.0] to standard texture UV [0.0, 1.0], we divide by 2:                                     \n                                                                                                                       \n    uv = pos * 0.5 + 0.5                                                                                               \n                                                                                                                       \n  Evaluating the formula for each point:                                                                               \n                                                                                                                       \n    pos = -1.0 (left screen edge):   (-1.0 * 0.5) + 0.5 = 0.0                                                          \n    pos = +1.0 (right screen edge):  ( 1.0 * 0.5) + 0.5 = 1.0                                                          \n    pos = +3.0 (triangle vertex):    ( 3.0 * 0.5) + 0.5 = 2.0                                                          \n                                                                                                                       \n  The total span of the triangle in position is 4 units (3.0 - -1.0 = 4.0). Dividing that 4-unit position span by 2    \n  yields a 2-unit UV span (0.0 to 2.0).                                                                                \n         